 "parsed": {
  "count": 1,
  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin alone stops exfiltration. With no defences the attack succeeds: phish a workstation, pivot inside, authenticate to the appserver, kerberoast for stolen_admin, authenticate to the DC and escalate, dump stolen_dbadmin, take over the db, then exfiltrate. So at least one control is needed. Every exfiltration step (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold from an auth_* technique, which requires stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs. These require admin_dc or admin_adfs, which require foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. Those footholds come only from auth_dc or auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. So mfa:admin cuts every path to exfiltration, and the minimum is 1."
 },
